# fixtures/hex/chain/corrupt/log.1.hex: store E ([F05 §5.3]). Commits c1, c2 and c3, each in its own durable
# group, all below durable_lsn. One bit of c2's message was flipped after the write (a media error the fault
# model allows, [F15]): c2's record checksum fails at a boundary below durable_lsn, so the store is corrupt:
# exit 7 naming log.1 and `moirai repair` ([F19]); the process never truncates below durable_lsn. c3's group
# after it is valid behind c2's original bytes, which shows that validity is checked group by group from the
# scan's start and a later valid group does not repair an earlier one.

